Project Description
This project is designed to convert power from the solar panels connected to J2 and J3, and deliver the output through J1.

U1 is a voltage regulator.

U2A works as an inverter.

U2G provides power to the inverter.

The output voltage is 3.3 V or 5 V.

Challenges
The main challenge was that the solar panels produced a fluctuating voltage. To stabilize it, we added a regulator, which required additional supporting circuitry.

Note: The power traces carry too little current to require a width increase.
